.TH APPIMAGE 1 "2024-11-14" "AppImage Launcher 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appimage \- AppImage Launcher CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appimage
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand options\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AppImage Launcher manages AppImages in ~/Applications (or a configured directory).
It provides a daemon that watches the directory, a CLI for manual operations,
and a D-Bus API for front-ends like the Aurelis Software Center.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Applications directory (default: ~/Applications)
.TP
\fB--json\fR
Output as JSON
.TP
\fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR
Suppress non-error output
.TP
\fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR
Increase verbosity (can be repeated)
.TP
\fB--no-color\fR
Disable colored output
.TP
\fB--no-daemon\fR
Force direct mode (bypass D-Bus)
.TP
\fB--version\fR
Show version
.TP
\fB--help\fR
Show help
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdaemon\fR
Run observer + D-Bus service in foreground (what systemd starts).
Options: \fB--dir\fR, \fB--no-notify\fR, \fB--no-dialogs\fR
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fIFILE\fR...
Install AppImage from any path. Already inside the dir = adopt in place.
Options:
.RS
.TP
\fB--name\fR \fINAME\fR
Managed name override
.TP
\fB--move\fR | \fB--copy\fR
Move or copy source file (default: copy)
.TP
\fB--replace\fR | \fB--keep\fR | \fB--cancel\fR | \fB--conflict-error\fR
Conflict policy
.TP
\fB--origin\fR \fIJSON\fR|\fB@\fR\fIFILE\fR
Origin record
.TP
\fB--silent\fR
Suppress success notification
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
Assume yes to prompts
.RE
.TP
\fBremove\fR \fINAME\fR...
Uninstall AppImage.
Options: \fB--keep-file\fR, \fB--purge\fR, \fB--yes\fR
.TP
\fBrename\fR \fINAME\fR \fINEW\fR
Rename AppImage; sets name_origin=user. \fB--reset\fR restores embedded Name=.
.TP
\fBlist\fR [\fB--json\fR] [\fB--sort\fR \fINAME\fR|\fISIZE\fR|\fIVERSION\fR|\fIDATE\fR] [\fB--all\fR]
Table of installed apps. \fB--all\fR includes kept/previous versions.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR \fINAME\fR|\fIFILE\fR [\fB--json\fR] [\fB--hash\fR]
Details of an app. If argument is a path to an uninstalled AppImage, prints metadata without installing.
.TP
\fBupdate\fR [\fINAME\fR|\fB--all\fR] [\fB--check\fR]
Check/apply zsync updates. \fB--check\fR exits 0 if none, 10 if updates exist.
.TP
\fBpolicy\fR \fINAME\fR \fIauto\fR|\fImanual\fR|\fIpinned\fR
Set update policy.
.TP
\fBorigin\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB--set\fR \fIJSON\fR|\fB@\fR\fIFILE\fR] [\fB--clear\fR]
Show, set or clear origin record.
.TP
\fBrevert\fR \fINAME\fR
Restore newest .previous version.
.TP
\fBversions\fR \fINAME\fR
List kept and previous versions.
.TP
\fBdisable\fR \fINAME\fR / \fBenable\fR \fINAME\fR
Convenience for uninstall/restore convention (moves to/from .disabled/).
.TP
\fBrun\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB--\fR \fIargs\fR]
Launch AppImage.
.TP
\fBbrowse\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB--exec-fallback\fR]
Mount read-only with squashfuse and open in Dolphin.
.TP
\fBextract\fR \fINAME\fR \fIDEST\fR
Extract squashfs (no execution).
.TP
\fBverify\fR \fINAME\fR
Re-validate file, signature, desktop entry, icon.
.TP
\fBreindex\fR
Run reconcile now.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Environment report: tools, bus, systemd, MIME, notifications, namespaces.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR \fIget\fR|\fIset\fR|\fIlist\fR
Read/write config.toml.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Daemon state, watched dir, pending conflicts/updates.
.TP
\fBcompletions\fR \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIfish\fR
Print completion script.
.TP
\fBexport\fR [\fIFILE\fR] / \fBimport\fR \fIFILE\fR
Export/import policies, names and flags as JSON.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
0
OK
.TP
1
Error
.TP
2
Usage/ambiguous name
.TP
3
Not found
.TP
4
Conflict needs a decision
.TP
5
Invalid or unsupported AppImage
.TP
6
Daemon required but unavailable
.TP
10
Updates available (update --check)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/Applications\fR
Default applications directory
.TP
\fI~/.config/appimage-launcher/config.toml\fR
User configuration
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/appimage-launcher/state.db\fR
State database
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/applications/appimage-*.desktop\fR
Desktop entries
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps/appimage-*.png\fR
Icons
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR appimage-launcher (7),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR dbus (1)
